v0.2.0:
    - Added plot saving with Ghostscript
    - Renamed Parameter.constraint to Parameter.setting
    - Various small fixes

v0.2.1:
    - Configuration is now settable during runtime

v0.3.0:
    - New Model class
    - AVLWrapper can now read an AVL input-file

v0.3.1:
    - Merged bufixes from Dario Isola & Phil Chiu

v0.3.2:
    - Bugfix for AIRFOIL keyword

v0.3.3:
    - Lots of bugfixes:
        - Creating Body while parsing inputfiles
        - RegEx bug in ElementFileReader (Thomas Greenhill)
        - Handling large numbers in tables
        - Handling stripforces with index > 99
        - Missing values now replaced with NaN instead of messing up the table format
          (columns were incorrectly shifted in previous versions)
        - Name labels incorrectly read in SurfaceFileReader
        - Type errors (mixing up floats & ints) while reading and writing files
          (AVL usually handles correcntly, but huge gain for consistency)
    - Case can now be read from input file
    - Spacing now parsed correctly
    - Two Spacials can now be added
    - Spacial can be multiplied/divived with a number
    - Added _underscore to separate control name from derivative (CYuelevator => CYu_elevator)
    - Added tests cases

v0.3.4:
    - Support multiple cases in 1 input file
    - Added body forces output
  ! - Cases are now indexed by number instead of name, since names are not required to be unique

v0.4.0:
    - Added mass distribution input
    - Added eigen-mode analysis and system matrix output

V0.4.1:
    - Lots of bugfixes:
        - Profile drag (CDCL) on more than one section was dropped or crashed
          while parsing input files
        - Negative masses were dropped while parsing mass files
        - Mass modifiers on masses without inertia
        - Malformed BODY header now raises an InputError
        - Unreadable error messages of InputError
        - Configuration.local_copy() now copies to the current working directory
        - Ghostscript output path
    - importing avlwrapper no longer requires tkinter
    - Single exception hierarchy, available as avlwrapper.AvlError, InputError,
      AvlExecutionError and OutputError
    - AVL failures are detected and raise an AvlExecutionError with the AVL output
    - Session accepts a timeout
    - Plots can be saved to a directory with the output_dir argument
    - Added Case.validate(), a Case can be printed without a Session
  ! - Session no longer modifies the given cases, use Session.cases to get the
      cases as used in the run
  ! - Unknown keywords in a Case which are not a control of the geometry now
      raise an InputError when running the Session
  ! - Eigenvalues are now indexed by case number as int instead of str
  ! - The AVL executable is no longer searched for in sys.path
  ! - PrintOutput prints the AVL output after the run instead of during the run
